if "the problem" is still that -lgfortran is not found, then in fact this will 
not change anything. See this thread 
http://sourceforge.net/forum/forum.php?thread_id=1883207&forum_id=165574 
(among others) for suggestions on working around this. In general, I believe 
installing g++, gcc, and gfortran in version 4.2 should do the trick.

Even with that solved, the "--ignore-missing-info" parameter will lead to 
problems building a .deb on ubuntu. See 
http://thread.gmane.org/gmane.comp.statistics.rkward.devel/88/focus=89 and 
the follow-up mail.

Meik Michalke has prepared a .deb for ubuntu gutsy and i386 (thanks!). I've 
uploaded this to:

http://rkward.sourceforge.net/temp/rkward_0.4.9gutsy1-1_i386.changes
http://rkward.sourceforge.net/temp/rkward_0.4.9gutsy1-1_i386.deb

